INSERT INTO notable_npcs (slug, name, real_name, title, system, race, occ, level, alignment, age, height, weight, attributes, hp, sdc, mdc, ppe, isp, ar, horror_factor, combat, bonuses_note, skills, skills_note, natural_abilities, magic, psionics, super_powers, cybernetics, weapons_and_equipment, money, disposition, allies, enemies, description, source_book) VALUES
('hell-lord-rune', 'Hell Lord Rune', 'Sonja Kerram (true name); also known as Commander Kerram and the Iron Lady', 'Hell Lord, commander of the Iron Guardsmen', 'rifts', 'Succubus (Lesser Demon of Hades), secretly a daughter of the evil god Ahriman', '10th level Succubus/schemer/seductress (as printed)', 10, 'Aberrant', '25', '6 feet (1.8 m)', '160 pounds (72 kg)', '{"IQ":17,"ME":17,"MA":20,"PS":26,"PP":24,"PE":18,"PB":26,"Spd":94}', 100, 60, 246, 144, NULL, 15, 15, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":6,"strike":7,"parry":10,"dodge":10,"entangle":2,"pull":7,"roll":5}', 'M.D.C. 246 without her armor; Soul Steel adds 1,000 more. Hit Points 100, S.D.C. 60 and A.R. 15 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures, where the armor has 1,000 S.D.C. Spd 94, doubled to 188 in Soul Steel. Seven attacks, eight with an energy rifle, and two more while she wears Soul Steel. The printed bonuses already include her attributes and the Rune armor: also +6 to strike with thrown weapons, knockout/stun on an unmodified 17-20, +6 to save vs Horror Factor, +5 vs magic, +3 vs psionics and +1 on all other saves. Supernatural P.S. 26. Horror Factor 15 comes from her reputation and ruthlessness.', '[{"name":"Camouflage","pct":63},{"name":"Climbing","pct":73},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":78},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":73},{"name":"Detect Concealment","pct":43},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":74},{"name":"Literacy: American","pct":83},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":90},{"name":"Military: Tanks & APCs","pct":73},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Robots & Power Armor","pct":77},{"name":"Sensory Equipment","pct":83},{"name":"Seduction","pct":92},{"name":"Swimming","pct":83},{"name":"Tracking","pct":68},{"name":"Weapon Systems","pct":88}]', 'Every Succubus skill plus those learned as a mercenary; these are the ones printed. Climbing is printed 73%/63% and the first figure is kept. Printed as Lore: Demons and Monsters, Pilot Tanks & APCs, Robots and Power Armor and Swimming; those carry their catalog names. Literacy: American has no catalog row, and Tracking is printed without saying of what. Also printed without a percentage: Kick Boxing, Paired Weapons, Robot Combat: Elite for the SAMAS and the X-10 Predator, and W.P. Energy Rifle at 5th level proficiency.', 'As the Succubus demon (Rifts Dimension Book 10: Hades p.60), with greater M.D.C. Fire and cold do her half damage. Heals 1D6x5 M.D.C. each melee round by Bio-Regeneration. Super Swift. Charm/impress 80%. She changes her looks at will but always as an attractive woman, and cannot copy a particular person. Vulnerabilities: silver weapons do their S.D.C. damage to her as M.D., and magic and magic weapons do full damage. She underestimates demon rivals and Deevils, has come to think herself indestructible in her armor, and her drive to free her father may cost her everything.', 'As the Succubus. P.P.E. 144. The spells of Soul Steel''s five pieces belong to the armor (its own gear row), not to her.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Soul Steel, a Greatest Rune Armor and her prize, held in the catalog as its own gear row (soul-steel): five pieces (helmet, chest plate, two gauntlets and greaves) adding 1,000 M.D.C. She also keeps a CP-50 Dragonfire rifle and a Death Bringer sword taken in the same Tolkeen raid, and has access to Techno-Wizard and demon weapons. Her stolen X-10 Predator and SAMAS power armor now go to other members of the company.', 'Once spent as fast as it came; now every resource goes into building and keeping her army. Her most valuable possession remains Soul Steel.', 'Rash, ruthless and hungry for power, but sharp: she reads what drives people and how to tempt them, and is a practised seductress who works men best of all. Unlike most demons she rarely underestimates humans or D-Bees, though she overrates herself, and since learning who her father is she counts herself above Greater Demons and Deevils. She will lie, cheat or kill for what she wants, yet a promise given on her honor is never broken.', 'The original core of the Iron Guardsmen and some of her new demon troops. Andras, the Marquis of Hades, whom she now owes a favor. Her father Ahriman, for only as long as she is useful to him.', 'The Coalition States, which put a 10 million credit bounty on her and the whole company; Tolkeen resistance fighters and Retribution Squads; most Greater Demons, who resent her rise; and every Hell Lord and ruler of Hades except Andras, who think she bought the title. Deevils and her demonic rivals, a list that grows with each victory.', 'A Succubus who spent three thousand years among mortals passing as human, she ran a power-armor mercenary company, the Iron Guardsmen, through the Siege on Tolkeen. Denied a Rune armor she had helped recover, she sold Tolkeen out to the Coalition and robbed the vault in the chaos, earning a place on the CS list of its twenty worst enemies and a ban from every merc market on the continent. The armor, Soul Steel, bought her a Hell Lord''s title and a demon army from Hades. Beheading a Raksasha general who tried to take her company won her his troops and the backing of Andras. Unknown to anyone, she is a child of the imprisoned god Ahriman, who guides her through dreams toward seizing the Deevil citadel Tower Grim so that he can go free, and will discard her afterward. Her army keeps the Iron Guardsmen''s name and silver-armor-on-black standard: the original mercenaries are her personal guard, and she means half her force to be humans, D-Bees and monsters hired, tempted or bought. It camps in the Magic Zone near the Devil''s Gate while she digs a Hell Pit there.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.67-69'),
('hell-lord-zugard', 'Hell Lord Zugard', 'Ojen Shid (true name); also known as Hell Lord Death and the Death-Bringer', 'Hell Lord of the New Mexico Hell Pit', 'rifts', 'Gallu Demon Bull (Greater Demon of Hades), partly inhabited by Death of the Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse', '7th level demonic hybrid and avatar of the Death Horseman of the Apocalypse (as printed)', 7, 'Miscreant', 'Effectively Immortal', 'Changes size at will; most comfortable at 14 feet (4.2 m)', 'Three tons', '{"IQ":17,"ME":10,"MA":22,"PS":46,"PP":20,"PE":18,"PB":4,"Spd":20}', 250, 400, 1600, 360, NULL, 12, 16, '{"attacks":8,"initiative":4,"strike":6,"parry":7,"dodge":6,"pull":5,"roll":4}', 'M.D.C. 1,600, ten times that once Death takes full possession of him. Hit Points 250, S.D.C. 400 and A.R. 12 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures. Saves as printed: +8 vs Horror Factor, +5 vs magic, impervious to psionics. Supernatural P.S. 46. W.P. Archery, Axe, Energy Rifles, Heavy M.D. Weapons and Pole Arm. Sunlight halves his Spd, attacks, combat bonuses and natural abilities. His armor adds +2 to Horror Factor.', '[{"name":"Barter","pct":78},{"name":"Brewing","pct":74},{"name":"Camouflage","pct":69},{"name":"Detect Ambush","pct":89},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":74},{"name":"Herding Cattle","pct":69},{"name":"Horsemanship: Exotic Animals","pct":79},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":80},{"name":"Lore: Cattle & Animals","pct":69},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":74},{"name":"Philosophy","pct":94},{"name":"Physiology","pct":74},{"name":"Pick Locks","pct":74},{"name":"Prowl","pct":84},{"name":"Skin & Prepare Animal Hides","pct":89},{"name":"Tailing","pct":74},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":79}]', 'Skills of note only. Brewing is printed 74%/79% and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals 79%/69%; the first figure is kept. Printed as Lore: Cattle/Animals, Lore: Demons and Monsters and Skin and Prepare Animal Hides (with a doubled percent sign); those carry their catalog names. Physiology has no catalog row and keeps the printed name.', 'Supernatural Strength and Endurance. Impervious to mind control, psionics and disease, the Hell Plagues included. Fire and cold do half damage, magic fire and cold included. Nightvision 2,000 feet (610 m). Heals 4D6 M.D.C. each melee round by Bio-Regeneration. Once a day he can call up and rule either 1D6 Death Demons, 1D6 Banshees, 2D6 Ghouls or 2D6 Nasu. Dimensional Teleport 80%. Speaks and understands all languages by magic. A bite or a blood-drawing claw strike can pass on the virus that turns its victim into a Death Demon (save of 14 or better). Vulnerabilities: silver-coated S.D.C. weapons do their M.D. equivalent (double damage in S.D.C. settings); holy weapons do double damage, holy water 2D6 M.D. a dose and 1D6x10 M.D. a gallon; wood from Millennium Trees does quadruple damage (triple to Hit Points in S.D.C. settings); ordinary M.D. weapons and magic do full damage; sunlight halves him as above.', 'Animate and Control Dead (20), Armor Bizarre (15), Aura of Death (12), Aura of Doom (40), Necromancy: Command Ghouls (10), Death Curse (Special), Deathword (70), Necromancy: Kill Plants (10), Life Drain (25), Necromancy: Maggots (20), Minor Curse (35), Orb of Cold (6), Paralysis: Lesser (5), Repel Animals (7), Shadow of Death (45), Shadow Meld (10), Shadow of Doom (45), Sickness (50), Spoil (30), Soultwist (170), Turn Dead (6) and Weight of Duty (10). P.P.E. 360.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A full suit of black magic plate armor trimmed in glowing red: 500 M.D.C., regenerating 1D4x10 per minute; +2 to Horror Factor, and it shields him from location magic such as Calling and Locate and from the psionic equivalents. His favourite weapon is a giant Rune pole arm whose shaft is a single bone and whose serrated cleaver blade carries three skulls: 1D6x10 M.D., all eight Rune weapon abilities, I.Q. 13, Miscreant, and the Necromancy spells Animate and Control Dead: Simple, Death Bolt, Necromancy: Command Ghouls, Necromancy: Death Strike, Grip of Death, Rattling Bones and Necromancy: Stench of the Dead, each five times a day at sixth level strength.', 'A hoard of metals, gems, jewelry and art from conquered worlds easily worth a billion credits, plus a small sack of 4D6x10,000 in gems he always carries. Death himself cares nothing for wealth.', 'Aloof even among demons, because he believes he now serves something greater. Finishing the Hell Pit, admitting his patron and keeping the bargain are all that matter to him. He stays calm in the worst fighting and has stopped fearing death.', 'His Death Demons, Banshees and Ghouls obey him without question; the rest of his troops sense something wrong and serve from fear or their own love of slaughter. The Demon Lords take him for a servant of Prince Ba''Zal. In truth he serves Death, and through him the other three Horsemen. Succor-Bemoth has offered Magots for his army in trade for Death Demons to study, which Death is weighing as a way into Succor-Bemoth''s holdings.', 'The other Hell Lords keep him at a distance, wary of his strength without guessing what he has become. As the vessel of Death he is the enemy of all life: mortals, demons and Deevils alike.', 'A Gallu Demon Bull sent to Earth as a Hell Lord days after he was infected while putting down rebel Death Demons, he hid his rotting from his officers and wandered in agony looking for a cure. A voice in his head eased the pain and finally drew him to its lair, where he agreed to help it return to this world in exchange for being made whole, a promise it never meant to keep. The voice was Death, one of the Apocalypse''s Four Horsemen (Rifts World Book Four: Africa), which put part of its essence into him. His horns have rotted away and his face is a death''s head over a starved frame, but his strength and mind are intact. Death means to take the New Mexico Hell Pit the moment it opens and use it to bring the Horsemen back, turning Zugard fully into Death; slaying him before then ends the threat. Until then he keeps a low profile. His army, the Army of Hell Lord Zugard/Death, holds more Death Demons than anywhere else on the planet and fights a scorched-earth war from New Mexico, taking prisoners only as laborers, food or new Death Demons.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.72-75'),
('hell-lord-fury', 'Hell Lord Fury', 'Ziur Y''Reffej (true name)', 'Hell Lord, commander of the Terror Army', 'rifts', 'Gallu Demon Bull (Greater Demon of Hades), remade as a Gallu-Centaur on a living bio-mechanical bull body', '11th level (as printed); his fellow Gallu-Centaurs are 1D6+4', 11, 'Diabolic', 'Effectively Immortal', '18 feet, 6 inches (5.6 m) tall and 20 feet (6.1 m) long', '5 tons', '{"IQ":14,"ME":16,"MA":20,"PS":42,"PP":20,"PE":20,"PB":8,"Spd":200}', 260, 300, 720, 90, NULL, 14, 17, '{"attacks":9,"initiative":5,"strike":6,"parry":8,"dodge":10,"pull":4,"roll":3}', 'P.S. 42 and P.P. 20 are his flesh right arm (Supernatural); his mechanical left arm and legs are Robot P.S. 45 and P.P. 25. Spd 200 running (135 mph/216 km). M.D.C. 720 is the flesh upper body; each of four bio-mechanical legs has 350 and the lower bull body 900. Hit Points 260, S.D.C. 300 and A.R. 14 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures, where the lower body has 500 S.D.C. and A.R. 17. P.P.E. 90 cannot be drawn on in this form. Also 60% trust/intimidate, +5 to save vs Horror Factor, +1 vs psionics/insanity and +5 vs magic. W.P. Axe, Chain, Energy Rifle and Heavy Mega-Damage Weapons.', '[{"name":"Climbing","pct":88},{"name":"Computer Operation","pct":78},{"name":"Dance","pct":98},{"name":"Horsemanship: Exotic Animals","pct":98},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Land Navigation","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Dragonese/Elven","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Demongogian","pct":98},{"name":"Literacy: Splugorth","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":98},{"name":"Lore: Faeries & Creatures of Magic","pct":78},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Swimming","pct":98},{"name":"Tracking (people)","pct":68},{"name":"Wilderness Survival","pct":88}]', 'Skills of note only. Climbing is printed 88%/78% and Horsemanship: Exotic Animals 98%/88%; the first figure is kept. Printed as Literate in Dragonese, Demongogian and Splugorth, Lore: Faeries, Math: Basic, Swim and Track (people); those carry their catalog names. Demongogian and Splugorth literacy have no catalog row.', 'Supernatural P.S. in the right arm, Robotic Strength 45 in the left arm and legs. Leaps 120 feet (36.6 m) lengthwise or 50 feet (15.2 m) up. Prowl 74%; moves silently at 40 mph (64 km) or less. Nightvision 90 feet (27.4 m) and sees the invisible. The flesh upper body Bio-Regenerates 2D6+2 per melee round; the bio-mechanical body 4D6 M.D.C. per melee (the features list prints 2D6+2) and regrows a lost leg in 2D4 hours. Impervious to heat, fire and toxic gases, though energy blasts and magical fire still hurt him fully. Speaks and understands all languages by magic at 96%. Dimensional Teleport 84%, and other Gallu-Centaurs within 1,000 feet (305 m) working with him share that figure in place of their own 30%; riders go with them. Runs through the air up to 100 feet (30.5 m) high and across water. Sixteen spikes on legs and chest can be plucked as hand weapons or launched, regrowing in 1D4 hours. Cannot cast spells or channel magic any longer, though he keeps a Gallu''s knowledge of it. Vulnerable as any Gallu, to holy weapons and demon-slaying magic among the rest. Losing the lower body, or leaving it, kills him within minutes, and it is not known whether he would return to Hades.', 'None usable. He keeps the spell knowledge of a Gallu Demon Bull but can no longer cast or channel magic.', NULL, NULL, 'Bio-mechanical features, each roughly the cybernetic feature of that name: Amplified Hearing, Radio Ear, Universal Headjack and Ear Implant, Sound Filtration System, a Climb Cord in the left hand holding 6 tons, an energized ball and chain on the left arm, the mechanical bull or horse lower body, and a small storage compartment in it. Two retractable hip energy cannons, 50 M.D.C. each, hit only by a Called Shot at -3, regrowing in 2D4 hours. A Multi-Optics left eye with a built-in laser. All of it is living, bonded flesh and machine, not true cybernetics, and heals at 2D6+2 M.D.C. per melee round.', 'Relies mostly on the weapons grown into him, but like any Greater Demon prizes magic weapons and items, Rune weapons and anything that hits hard.', 'More in assets than coin: Charun has put him in command of a large force of Kreelock-built vehicles and equipment.', 'Once a glory-loving brawler who relished blood and battle, he spent years wanting only to be restored, and he and his Gallu-Centaurs poured that rage into ever more savage fighting. Mocked and feared by other Greater Demons but revered by lesser demons, Fallen and many Lesser Deevils, he now wonders whether the change was fate, and gathers followers so that he can one day claim a Demon Lord''s place, starting with Rifts Earth.', 'The Taursis worship him as a god who can raise their station and would die for him, though he has not accepted them as his minions; other outcast Lesser Demons follow him too, many as volunteers. Charun the Cruel, the one Demon Lord who deals with him, lends him Gargoyles. Humans and most non-demons are tools to him.', 'Deevils above all, whom he blames for what happened to him. The Demon Lords who turned their backs on him, Modeus among them, he now counts as rivals to bring down. Other Greater Demons envy and distrust him more as he grows.', 'A Gallu Demon Bull captain who led from the front, Fury was boarding a Deevil starship when its magic reactor blew, flinging survivors through a Rift into a dimension of machines. Swarms of small robots rebuilt the dying demons: Fury woke with a living mechanical bull body in place of his lost legs and lower half, a mechanical left arm, and a voice in his head, and teleported out with 23 of his altered Gallu before it could take them. Cutting the machine parts away kills a Gallu-Centaur, so Hades spared them and, to be rid of them, made him a Hell Lord and sent him to Earth. He hates the body, which makes him look like the lowly Taursis. His army, renamed Terror Reborn but called the Terror Army, is mechanized cavalry: three dozen Walking Death and Carnage Tanks break the enemy, then fast demons, Taursis and war machines ride in, about half armed with bone weapons, under a red flag with a charging black bull. He is building several Hell Pits in the ruins of Detroit and Windsor and is likely to strike New Lazlo first.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.77-80'),
('hell-lord-siren', 'Hell Lord Siren', 'Tih''we R''Toyla (true name)', 'Hell Lord, agent of Queen Mania, commander of Siren''s Call', 'rifts', 'Succubus (Lesser Demon of Hades) raised to Hell Lord', '9th level Seductress, new to being a general and Hell Lord (as printed)', 9, 'Miscreant', 'Effectively Immortal', 'Varies, 4 to 16 feet (1.2 to 4.9 m)', NULL, '{"IQ":20,"ME":17,"MA":24,"PS":24,"PP":20,"PE":18,"PB":30,"Spd":14}', 174, 180, 450, 144, 62, 12, 14, '{"attacks":7,"initiative":2,"strike":5,"parry":5,"dodge":5,"disarm":3,"pull":4,"roll":4}', 'M.D.C. 450. Hit Points 174, S.D.C. 180 and A.R. 12 are the block''s S.D.C.-setting figures. P.B. 30 is her maximum; she sets it as she likes but never below 17. Spd 14 on foot, 132 flying (90 mph/144 km). Also +4 on Perception Rolls, +10 to save vs Horror Factor, +4 vs magic, +3 vs psionics and +3 vs all mind control, charms, illusion and possession. Angered or flustered, her Perception, initiative, skills and charm, intimidation and combat bonuses are halved. W.P. Energy Pistol, Knife, Sword and Paired Weapons. The block prints no punch or kick damage, and none is derived here.', '[{"name":"Barter","pct":98},{"name":"Begging","pct":98},{"name":"Dance","pct":92},{"name":"Escape Artist","pct":66},{"name":"Horsemanship: Exotic Animals","pct":72},{"name":"Hovercraft (Ground)","pct":86},{"name":"I.D. Undercover Agent","pct":92},{"name":"Impersonation","pct":78},{"name":"Intelligence","pct":98},{"name":"Interrogation","pct":92},{"name":"Lore: Demons & Monsters","pct":81},{"name":"Mathematics: Basic","pct":98},{"name":"Performance","pct":98},{"name":"Prowl","pct":72},{"name":"Public Speaking","pct":94},{"name":"Radio: Basic","pct":81},{"name":"Seduction","pct":92},{"name":"Sing","pct":91},{"name":"Streetwise","pct":50},{"name":"Undercover Ops","pct":98},{"name":"Wardrobe & Grooming","pct":80}]', 'Skills of note only. Horsemanship: Exotic Animals is printed 72/62%; the first figure is kept. Interrogation is usually through seduction. Printed as Math: Basic; that carries its catalog name. Hovercraft (Ground) has no catalog row and keeps the printed name.', 'As the Succubus, plus Supernatural Strength and Endurance. Flies to 30,000 feet (9,144 m). Nightvision 1,000 feet (305 m). Fire does half damage, magic fire included. Dimensional Teleport 64%. Speaks and understands all languages by magic at 96%. Heals 4D6 M.D.C. each melee by Bio-Regeneration, and regrows lost wings or limbs in 1D6+2 days. Hypnotic Voice: males find her voice alluring and are -2 to save against her charm, mind control and psionics; a charmed victim carries out a possible suggestion or answers truthfully, except under torture or threat, and one who saves is immune to the charm for 24 hours. Pheromone Attraction: three times a day, every male within 10 feet (3 m) saves vs magic at 15 or becomes infatuated, believing her, guarding her and treating other men as rivals; most women react the other way and distrust her. Shape Changer: any female humanoid of any species for as long as she likes, from 4 to 16 feet (1.2 to 4.9 m), but never a particular person and not convincing up close. Vulnerabilities: overconfident, especially with men, and cannot tell when a man only pretends to want her; women are unmoved and roll trust/intimidate at half; silver, and S.D.C. weapons, do their Mega-Damage equivalent (double damage in S.D.C. settings); double damage from sonic and sound-based attacks, a Glitter Boy''s Boom Gun included.', 'Gained with her rank: P.P.E. 144, each spell cast at 3rd level strength. Aura of Power (4), Calling (8), Charm (12), Charismatic Aura (10), Cloak of Darkness (6), Compulsion (20), Distant Voice (10), Domination (10), Escape (8), Fool''s Gold (10), Invisibility: Simple (6), Repel Animals (7), Trance (10) and Turn Dead (6).', 'Gained with her rank: I.S.P. 62. Alter Aura (2), Empathy (4), Hypnotic Suggestion (6), Mind Block (4), Sense Time (2) and Suppress Fear (8); she also uses Suppress Fear to put would-be lovers at ease.', NULL, NULL, 'A large wardrobe of leathers, silks, gowns and lingerie. For protection a Splugorth Talisman of Armor (100 M.D.C., three times a day, raising itself the moment she is attacked), and for a weapon a Splugorth Fang (4D6 M.D.). She means to charm her way to better gear, a Rune weapon most of all.', 'Very little: 10,000 in Modeus coins, which she expects to change soon.', 'She plays the innocent, bewildered girl so naturally that mortals and supernatural beings alike underestimate her, and has made the manipulation of men (and women, when needed) an art; when charm fails she turns to threats and violence, usually by someone else''s hand. Cool and calculating even under fire, she can still become a raging monster in an instant, usually in her true demon form, and that loss of control is when she is weakest. She lies and betrays without remorse and cares nothing for those hurt along the way. Queen Mania is perhaps the only being she trusts and honors. She has never loved and thinks love the worst lie of all.', 'Queen Mania, her patron, to whom she stays loyal. Many Succubi and Incubi in her army. Anyone else she can use, mortal, magical or supernatural, as pawns and playthings.', 'The Deevils first, and every enemy or rival of Queen Mania. The other newly made Hell Lords underestimate her, as she intends. Mortals, men above all, are hers to use and discard.', 'Queen Mania''s most trusted spy, raised to Hell Lord because Mania, shut out of the war councils and suspicious that her lover Charun was making allies behind her back, wanted her own agent in the race for Rifts Earth. New to the rank and to generalship, Siren is learning strategy fast and leans on what she knows: espionage, seduction and turning others against each other. She plans no Hell Pit yet; she means to set the other Hell Lords fighting each other, stir human and D-Bee revolts, and spy on every power in North America, with a rumor that Federation of Magic leader Alistair Dunscon may favour demons high on her list. Her small army, which she named Siren''s Call after herself, has little battle experience, arms itself with whatever comes to hand and wants Walking Death and Carnage Tanks; it flies a black and red triangle with a gold skull. Her command post is hidden in Ciudad Juarez among demons passing as humans and D-Bees, with a second camp for the rest in the Sierra Madre, and her spies are planted in each rival Hell Lord''s camp.', 'Rifts World Book 35: Megaverse in Flames p.81-84');
